          "guidance": "USU specifically distinguishes Florence fennel, grown for its swollen base, from common fennel grown mainly for foliage and seed. For established plants it recommends full sun and fertile, well-drained, moisture-retentive soil; letting the soil dry or fluctuate can contribute to bolting or split stalks. It reports 8–12 inches as outdoor soil thinning after bulbing begins; this is not indoor pod spacing. RHS says up to three mature plants can be grown in a container about 40 cm wide and cautions that containers dry rapidly, so regular moisture checks matter because drying can trigger bolting. The container advice is for soil-based growing and does not establish hydroponic suitability or pod spacing.",
