          "guidance": "Harvest immature pods while tender, commonly around 2–3 inches in UGA and UF/IFAS guidance; timing and acceptable size vary by cultivar. UGA reports harvest beginning roughly 60–70 days after planting in its regional home-garden guidance, while UF/IFAS recommends checking every two to three days in South Florida. Frequent picking prevents overmature, fibrous pods and supports continued production. Handle carefully: plant and pod spines can irritate skin, and branches are brittle.",
