          "guidance": "USU advises thorough, regular watering because celery has shallow roots; water stress can make stalks stringy and stronger-flavored. Its regional guide gives 55–65°F as an ideal crop range, says several weeks of cool exposure can trigger flowering, and advises closer watering above 85°F to limit stress and fiber development. These are outdoor crop references, not indoor-system setpoints. The source also warns that shallow cultivation can damage roots.",
