          "guidance": "NC State lists root cuttings and division. UMN recommends planting root cuttings in early spring once soil is workable; its one-foot spacing and two-to-three-inch cover are soil-row instructions and must not be treated as hydroponic pod spacing. The selected sources do not establish a seed-starting protocol for this represented root-propagated crop.",
