          "short": "In Minnesota, harvest in late fall before freeze or in spring",
          "guidance": "UMN's Minnesota guide delays fall harvest until late October or early November, just before the ground freezes, after late-summer and early-autumn root growth. It offers spring harvest as new growth begins when suitable cool storage is unavailable and notes roots left for two growing seasons may become stringy and woody. These are regional timing cues, not a universal calendar.",
